    <header>
        <h1>How to Cook Rice and Stew</h1>
        <p>A simple Nigerian-style rice and stew recipe</p>
    </header>

    <div class="container">

        <h2>Ingredients for the Rice</h2>

        <ul>
            <li>3 cups of long-grain rice</li>
            <li>6 cups of water</li>
            <li>1 teaspoon of salt</li>
            <li>1 tablespoon of vegetable oil (optional)</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Ingredients for the Stew</h2>

        <ul>
            <li>8 fresh tomatoes</li>
            <li>3 red bell peppers (Tatashe)</li>
            <li>2 Scotch bonnet peppers (Ata Rodo), or according to taste</li>
            <li>2 large onions</li>
            <li>1 kg of chicken or beef</li>
            <li>1 cup of vegetable oil</li>
            <li>2 tablespoons of tomato paste</li>
            <li>2 seasoning cubes</li>
            <li>1 teaspoon of curry powder</li>
            <li>1 teaspoon of thyme</li>
            <li>Salt to taste</li>
            <li>1 cup of meat stock</li>
            <li>2 cloves of garlic (optional)</li>
            <li>Small piece of ginger (optional)</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Step-by-Step Procedure for Cooking the Rice</h2>

        <div class="step">
            <h3>Step 1: Wash the Rice</h3>
            <p>
                Put the rice in a bowl and wash it several times with clean water
                until the water becomes relatively clear.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
            <h3>Step 2: Boil the Water</h3>
            <p>
                Pour 6 cups of water into a clean pot and bring it to a boil.
                Add salt and vegetable oil if desired.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
            <h3>Step 3: Add the Rice</h3>
            <p>
                Add the washed rice to the boiling water and stir gently.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
            <h3>Step 4: Cook the Rice</h3>
            <p>
                Cover the pot and allow the rice to cook on medium heat.
                Cook until the rice becomes soft and the water is absorbed.
                Add a little water if necessary.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
            <h3>Step 5: Serve the Rice</h3>
            <p>
                Once the rice is fully cooked, turn off the heat and allow it
                to rest for a few minutes before serving.
            </p>
        </div>

        <h2>Step-by-Step Procedure for Cooking the Stew</h2>

        <div class="step">
            <h3>Step 1: Prepare the Meat</h3>
            <p>
                Wash the chicken or beef and put it in a pot. Add chopped onions,
                salt, seasoning cubes, thyme and a little water. Cook until the
                meat is tender. Keep the meat stock for the stew.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
            <h3>Step 2: Prepare the Peppers and Tomatoes</h3>
            <p>
                Wash the tomatoes, red bell peppers, Scotch bonnet peppers and
                onions. Blend them together until smooth.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
            <h3>Step 3: Boil the Blended Mixture</h3>
            <p>
                Pour the blended tomatoes and peppers into a pot. Cook on medium
                heat until some of the excess water evaporates.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
            <h3>Step 4: Fry the Stew</h3>
            <p>
                Heat the vegetable oil in a clean pot. Add some sliced onions
                and fry for a few minutes. Add the tomato paste and fry briefly.
                Then add the cooked pepper and tomato mixture.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
            <h3>Step 5: Add Seasoning</h3>
            <p>
                Add curry powder, thyme, seasoning cubes and salt to taste.
                Stir everything together.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
            <h3>Step 6: Add the Meat Stock</h3>
            <p>
                Pour the meat stock into the stew and stir well. Allow the stew
                to cook on medium heat until the oil rises to the top and the
                stew becomes thick.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
            <h3>Step 7: Add the Meat</h3>
            <p>
                Add the cooked chicken or beef to the stew. Allow it to simmer
                for another 10 to 15 minutes so that the meat absorbs the flavor.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
            <h3>Step 8: Serve</h3>
            <p>
                Turn off the heat and serve the hot stew with the cooked rice.
                Enjoy your delicious homemade rice and stew!
            </p>
        </div>

        <h2>Serving Suggestion</h2>

        <p>
            Rice and stew can be served with fried plantain, boiled eggs,
            vegetables or a cold drink.
        </p>

    </div>

